# Pin Constraint File for iCE40-UP5K (UPduino v3.0 / iCEBreaker)
# FM Audio Transmitter Project
#
# This file provides pin assignments for common UP5K development boards
# Uncomment the section that matches your board
#
# Supported boards:
#   - UPduino v3.0
#   - iCEBreaker
#   - Other UP5K boards (adjust pins accordingly)

#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPduino v3.0 Pin Assignments
#---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Clock input (12 MHz onboard oscillator)
set_io clk_in 35

# Reset (active low) - Use button or GPIO
set_io rst_n 10

# UART Interface (using GPIO pins)
set_io uart_rx 12

# FM Antenna Output
set_io antenna 21

# Status LEDs (UPduino has RGB LED, using separate channels)
set_io led_locked 41      # Red channel
set_io led_configured 40  # Green channel
set_io led_active 39      # Blue channel

#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iCEBreaker Pin Assignments (Alternative - comment out UPduino section above)
#---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Uncomment for iCEBreaker board:
# set_io clk_in 35
# set_io rst_n 10
# set_io uart_rx 6
# set_io antenna 9
# set_io led_locked 11
# set_io led_configured 37
# set_io led_active 38

#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - Antenna wire: 10-15 cm for testing, ~75 cm for quarter-wave at 100 MHz
# - RGB LED pins may need external resistors depending on board
# - For UART, ensure voltage levels match (3.3V for UP5K)
# - Always verify pin assignments with your board schematic
